				<r3d:description language="eng">The Global Runoff Data Centre (GRDC) is an international data centre operating under the auspices of the World Meteorological Organization (WMO) at the Federal Institute of Hydrology, Koblenz, Germany. Established in 1988 to support the research on global and climate change and integrated water resources management, it holds the most substantive collection of quality assured river discharge data on global scale.</r3d:description>
